(969, 'Aretha Aultman', 'GPU bottlenecks explained', 'aultman.aretha@hotmail.com', '08175311274', 'The biggest mistake in PC building is mismatched CPU and GPU combinations. People overspend on one component and bottleneck the entire system, especially across 1080p, 1440p, and 4K scenarios.\r\n\r\nhttps://www.shooshmonkey.com/post/how-to-choose-the-right-pc-hardware\r\n\r\nThe article explains how performance shifts depending on resolution and workload, and why real-world FPS data is the only reliable way to validate a build. It reinforces that synthetic scores alone don’t reflect real gaming performance.\r\n\r\nIf your content covers PC builds, gaming, or hardware optimization, this is a strong supporting resource, it helps users avoid wasted budget and build properly balanced systems based on data\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nShould you prefer not to get additional notifications from our side, please fill the form at brnd .li/delist URL with your domain address (URL).\r\n34 Colorado Way, Hancock, CA, USA, 90019', '2026-07-22 23:43:15', '2026-07-22 23:43:15'),
